            <ArticleTitle>[Injection therapy in lumbar syndromes].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>922-31</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Injection therapy as part of orthopaedic pain treatment is of major importance in sciatica. It helps to differentiate unclear complaints and allows a break through of the vicious circle of pain and muscle spasm. Pharmacological principles and possible complications have to be observed. The different techniques need experience and manual training. The paper describes the various injection techniques in detail.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
